' Body of login-sequence.puml / login-sequence-dark.puml. No start marker, so
' PlantUML will not render this file directly, and naming one in a comment here
' breaks the include. See README.md.
'
' Order transcribed from services/session-lifecycle/src/handshake.rs. Why each
' step sits where it does: ../SERVICES.md §3.

skinparam defaultFontName Inter
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
' No ParticipantPadding: deprecated, and the warning is painted into the render.
skinparam BoxPadding 10

title One login, in murmur's order

header
Client-bound frames carry their <b>«type»</b> from the frame header; internal calls are gRPC.
Call graph: <b>service-graph.puml</b>.   Why this order: <b>SERVICES.md</b> §3.
endheader

actor "Mumble\nclient" as cl $c_client
participant "**gateway**" as gw $c_gw
participant "**session-**\n**lifecycle**" as sl $c_ess
box "read on the way through" $c_box
  participant "**server-**\n**config**" as cfg $c_hub
  participant "**userdata**" as ud $c_ess
  participant "**permissions**" as pm $c_hub
  participant "**metadata**" as md $c_ess
  participant "**voice**" as vc $c_core
  participant "**session-view**" as sv $c_hub
end box

== TLS ==

cl -> gw : TCP + TLS
gw ->> sl : `Opened` «conn, addr, cert hash, chain»
note over gw, sl $c_note
  Broadcast to every service. Only session-lifecycle acts on it.
end note
sl --> cl : **Version** «0»  · server-first
cl -> sl : **Version** «0»
cl -> sl : **Authenticate** «2»\nname · password · tokens · opus

== Admission ==

sl -> cfg : `Get`
cfg --> sl : settings snapshot
sl -> ud : `Authenticate`
ud --> sl : account · profile hashes

alt refused
  sl --> cl : **Reject** «4»\nWrongServerPw · NoCertificate\nUsernameInUse · ServerFull
  sl --> gw : `Disconnect`
end

== Landing ==

sl -> sv : `Announce` «session up»
note right of sl $c_note
  Before the landing: permissions resolves the session through session-view.
end note
sl -> md : `LastChannel`
sl -> pm : `CheckSession`
pm --> sl : verdict
sl -> sv : `Announce` «channel changed»

== Welcome ==

sl -> vc : `Mint`
vc --> sl : **CryptSetup** payload
note right of vc $c_note
  Voice mints it. Key material never leaves voice in a usable form.
end note
sl --> cl : **CryptSetup** «15»
sl --> cl : **CodecVersion** «21»
sl -> md : `GetTree`
md --> sl : every channel
sl --> cl : **ChannelState** «7» × N,\nbreadth-first from the root
sl --> cl : **UserState** «9», their own
sl -> sv : `List`
sv --> sl : every other live session
sl --> cl : **UserState** «9» × N
sl --> cl : **ServerSync** «5»
sl --> cl : **ServerConfig** «24»
sl --> cl : **SuggestConfig** «25»

== Session ==

sl ->> gw : `SessionUp` «conn -> session»
note over sl, gw $c_note
  The gateway learns conn -> session here and nowhere else.
end note
sl --> cl : **UserState** «9» to everyone **else**

== After the sync ==

sl -> md : `RestoreListeners`
md --> sl : their listeners
sl --> cl : **UserState** «9» carrying them
note right of sl $c_note
  After ServerSync, not before (`Messages.cpp:843`).
end note
sl -> pm : `Effective`
pm --> sl : permission set
sl --> cl : **PermissionQuery** «20»  · pushed, not requested

legend bottom
|= arrow |= meaning |
| solid | a request the sender waits on |
| dashed | a reply, or a frame written to the client |
| open head | fire and forget |
Client frames ride the reply half of `ClientPlane.Attach`. No service dials the gateway.
endlegend
